{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4mf6hb6waguk2n6ufxt25sxmmi3n6uhqlxosigg277sdydak76tq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01ScCjmBRWJjKCorPZ8VLMcN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-cvRa1v/translation/ERRORS.md","content":"# ERRORS.md — Phase A: error / rejection surface table\n\n## How this was derived (mechanically)\n\n```\n$ grep -n 'return\\|assert\\|if\\|NULL\\|ERROR\\|errno\\|<\\|>' c_src/src/*.c c_src/include/*.h\n```\n\nFindings, exhaustively:\n\n* **No** `assert` anywhere (`grep -c assert c_src -r` -> 0).\n* **No** `NULL` comparison anywhere (`grep -c NULL c_src -r` -> 0).\n* **No** error enum, no `errno`, no `RETURN_ERROR`-style macro, no `-1` /\n  `NULL` sentinel return. `grep -c 'return -1\\|return NULL' c_src -r` -> 0.\n* **No** `#if` / `#ifdef` conditional code.\n* The only named constant is `#define N_SMOOTH 16` (a divisor and a window\n  width, not a limit that is validated).\n* `match` has **exactly one** `if` statement, and it is the library's only\n  explicit rejection path: `return 0`.\n* Everything else that \"rejects\" input does so implicitly, through loop\n  guards (`i < length`), unguarded division, and unguarded pointer arithmetic.\n\nSo the error surface is: **one explicit rejection**, **one implicit rejection**\n(the final ordered comparison), and a set of unchecked-boundary behaviours that\nthe C exhibits rather than diagnoses. Every one of those is a row below,\nbecause each is a real input an external caller can supply across the FFI\nboundary, and the Rust must behave identically.\n\n`float_t` note that governs several rows: `match.c` sees `typedef double\nfloat_t` from `match.h`; `spectral_contrast.c` includes only `<math.h>` and\nnever `match.h`, so there `float_t` is glibc's `typedef float float_t`\n(verified on this host: `sizeof(float_t) == 4`, `FLT_EVAL_METHOD == 0`).\n`spectral_contrast` therefore indexes its arguments as `float`, including when\n`match` calls it with `double` buffers. That is the ground truth.\n\n## The table\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| E1 | `match` | `total(test,bins) < threshold * total(reference,bins)` — the energy gate at `match.c:37`, the library's only explicit `return 0`. Reached e.g. with `test` energy strictly below `threshold *` `reference` energy. | returns `0` (int), **before** any preprocessing; `test`/`reference` untouched |\n| E2 | `match` | gate operand is NaN, so the `<` is unordered: `total(test,bins)` is NaN, or `threshold` is NaN, or the product is NaN. `comisd`+`jbe` ⇒ unordered does **not** take the `return 0` branch. | gate does **not** reject; execution falls through to preprocessing |\n| E3 | `match` | `threshold * total(reference,bins)` = `inf * 0` or `0 * inf` (invalid op) ⇒ product is the x86 indefinite QNaN `0xFFF8000000000000` | gate unordered ⇒ falls through (same as E2) |\n| E4 | `match` | final `spectral_contrast(t,r,bins) >= threshold` is false or unordered (contrast NaN, or `threshold` NaN, or `threshold` = `+inf`). `comisd`+`setae`: unordered ⇒ CF=1 ⇒ 0. | returns `0` |\n| E5 | `match` | `bins == 0`. VLAs are zero-length; `total` loops 0×, so gate is `0.0 < threshold*0.0`; `memcpy(v,src,0)` is a no-op; `smoothen` loops 0×; **`differentiate` stores `v[-1] = 0` out of bounds** (`match.c:25`, unguarded). | no crash (the OOB store lands in `match`'s own zero-sized alloca scratch, below `%rsp`); returns `(0.0 >= threshold)`, i.e. `1` iff `threshold <= 0.0`, `0` if `threshold > 0.0` or NaN |\n| E6 | `spectral_contrast` | `length == 0` | all three loops run 0×; `sqrt(0.0)` never used; returns `+0.0`; both arrays untouched |\n| E7 | `spectral_contrast` | `length < 0` (e.g. `-1`, `-1000`, `INT_MIN`) — no validation; every loop guard `i < length` is false at `i = 0` | returns `+0.0`; both arrays untouched; **no** crash |\n| E8 | `match` | `bins < 0` — no validation. Gate passes (totals are `0.0`), then `preprocess` calls `memcpy(v, source, length * sizeof(*v))` where `length * sizeof` converts a **negative int to `size_t`** ⇒ ~2^64-sized copy. | **segfault** (UB in the C; not a value the C \"returns\"). Documented, not asserted for value equality; see `tests/errors.rs::e8_negative_bins_documented` |\n| E9 | `spectral_contrast` / `normalize` | zero magnitude: `dot_product(v,v,length) == 0` ⇒ `magnitude == 0.0` ⇒ `v[i] /= 0.0` with **no guard** (`spectral_contrast.c:13`). Happens for an all-`+0.0`/`-0.0` array, and *always* inside `match` when `preprocess` output is all zeros (e.g. constant input spectra). | `0.0/0.0` ⇒ indefinite QNaN `0xFFC00000` (f32); `x/0.0` for `x != 0` ⇒ `±inf` (f32). Then `dot_product` of those ⇒ `NaN`. `match` then returns `0` (E4). No crash. |\n| E10 | `spectral_contrast` / `normalize` | negative-`dot_product` self-product is impossible in exact math, but with the f32 reinterpretation `sum` can become `-inf`/NaN ⇒ `sqrt` of NaN/negative | `sqrt(NaN)` ⇒ quieted NaN; `sqrt` never sees a negative finite value because `a[i]*a[i] >= 0`, but it can see `NaN`. Propagates; no crash |\n| E11 | `spectral_contrast` | `a[i]` / `b[i]` bytes decode to an **f32 signalling NaN** (`0x7FBFFFFF` etc.). No check; `mulss`/`cvtss2sd`/`divsd` quiet it. | quieted NaN propagated (payload rules in `src/lib.rs`); result NaN; no trap (SSE exceptions masked) |\n| E12 | `spectral_contrast` | aliased arguments `spectral_contrast(v, v, length)` — permitted by C (no `restrict`), so `normalize` runs **twice** on the same buffer | second `normalize` divides the already-normalized data by ≈1.0; result ≈ `1.0`; buffer mutated twice |\n| E13 | `spectral_contrast` | partially overlapping arguments, e.g. `spectral_contrast(v, v+1, length-1)` | well-defined in C: `normalize(a)` completes before `normalize(b)` starts; must match byte-for-byte |\n