. | `e14_null_pointers` | [x] |\n| E15 | both | out-of-range value across the FFI boundary. **The API declares no `enum`**, so the exhaustive integer surface is `int bins` / `int length`; the whole `int` range is accepted without validation. Boundaries: `INT_MIN`, `INT_MIN+1`, `-2`, `-1`, `0`, `1`, `INT_MAX`, and a stack-exhausting `4_000_000`. | `spectral_contrast`: `INT_MIN..=0` ⇒ exactly `+0.0` (both); `1` ⇒ values compared over 50 random inputs; `INT_MAX` ⇒ both fault, asserted equal. `match`: `1` ⇒ compared over 50 random inputs; `INT_MIN`/`INT_MIN+1`/`-1`/`0` ⇒ SIGSEGV in C (asserted); `4_000_000` ⇒ C exhausts the 8 MB stack with its two 32 MB VLAs and dies (asserted), Rust heap-allocates and survives (documented divergence on an input C cannot handle). | `e15_integer_boundaries` | [x] |\n| E16 | `match` | `bins == 1`: `differentiate`'s loop body never runs (`1 - 1 == 0`), so the trailing `v[0] = 0` makes **both** preprocessed buffers all-zero ⇒ E9. `spectral_contrast` then reads **1 f32** out of the 2 f32 slots of the single `double`. | contrast is NaN ⇒ `>= threshold` false ⇒ returns `0` for **every** threshold; asserted to be exactly `0` as well as equal, across all 21 threshold classes and 200 random raw-bit inputs | `e16_match_bins_one_zeroed_by_differentiate` | [x] |\n| E17 | both | `bins` / `length` odd, so `spectral_contrast` reads `bins` f32 slots = `bins/2` whole doubles plus the low half of one more — never past the end of the `bins`-double buffer, since `bins <= 2*bins`. This is the exact boundary the `float_t` confusion sits on. | in bounds; no crash; value and both buffers must match | `e17_odd_bins_f32_view_boundary` | [x] |\n| E18 | `smoothen` | window clamped at the array end (`i + j < length`) while the divisor stays `N_SMOOTH` = 16, unguarded — the last `min(15, length-1)` outputs are attenuated by `(length-i)/16`. For `length < 16` **every** element is attenuated. | attenuated tail, bit-exact. **Correction to a natural but wrong assumption:** this means a *constant* spectrum does NOT preprocess to all zeros (e.g. `[7.5, 7.5]` → `[0.9375, 0.46875]` → `[-0.46875, 0]` → `[-0.029296875, 0]`), so it does *not* reach the zero-magnitude path; only an all-zero spectrum does. | `e18_smoothen_attenuated_tail` | [x] |","originalFile":"# ERRORS.md — Phase A: error / rejection surface table\n\n## How this was derived (mechanically)\n\n```\n$ grep -n 'return\\|assert\\|if\\|NULL\\|ERROR\\|errno\\|<\\|>' c_src/src/*.c c_src/include/*.h\n```\n\nFindings, exhaustively:\n\n* **No** `assert` anywhere (`grep -c assert c_src -r` -> 0).\n* **No** `NULL` comparison anywhere (`grep -c NULL c_src -r` -> 0).\n* **No** error enum, no `errno`, no `RETURN_ERROR`-style macro, no `-1` /\n  `NULL` sentinel return. `grep -c 'return -1\\|return NULL' c_src -r` -> 0.\n* **No** `#if` / `#ifdef` conditional code.\n* The only named constant is `#define N_SMOOTH 16` (a divisor and a window\n  width, not a limit that is validated).\n* `match` has **exactly one** `if` statement, and it is the library's only\n  explicit rejection path: `return 0`.\n* Everything else that \"rejects\" input does so implicitly, through loop\n  guards (`i < length`), unguarded division, and unguarded pointer arithmetic.\n\nSo the error surface is: **one explicit rejection**, **one implicit rejection**\n(the final ordered comparison), and a set of unchecked-boundary behaviours that\nthe C exhibits rather than diagnoses. Every one of those is a row below,\nbecause each is a real input an external caller can supply across the FFI\nboundary, and the Rust must behave identically.\n\n`float_t` note that governs several rows: `match.c` sees `typedef double\nfloat_t` from `match.h`; `spectral_contrast.c` includes only `<math.h>` and\nnever `match.h`, so there `float_t` is glibc's `typedef float float_t`\n(verified on this host: `sizeof(float_t) == 4`, `FLT_EVAL_METHOD == 0`).\n`spectral_contrast` therefore indexes its arguments as `float`, including when\n`match` calls it with `double` buffers. That is the ground truth.\n\n## The table\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| E1 | `match` | `total(test,bins) < threshold * total(reference,bins)` — the energy gate at `match.c:37`, the library's only explicit `return 0`. Reached e.g. with `test` energy strictly below `threshold *` `reference` energy. | returns `0` (int), **before** any preprocessing; `test`/`reference` untouched |\n| E2 | `match` | gate operand is NaN, so the `<` is unordered: `total(test,bins)` is NaN, or `threshold` is NaN, or the product is NaN. `comisd`+`jbe` ⇒ unordered does **not** take the `return 0` branch. | gate does **not** reject; execution falls through to preprocessing |\n| E3 | `match` | `threshold * total(reference,bins)` = `inf * 0` or `0 * inf` (invalid op) ⇒ product is the x86 indefinite QNaN `0xFFF8000000000000` | gate unordered ⇒ falls through (same as E2) |\n| E4 | `match` | final `spectral_contrast(t,r,bins) >= threshold` is false or unordered (contrast NaN, or `threshold` NaN, or `threshold` = `+inf`). `comisd`+`setae`: unordered ⇒ CF=1 ⇒ 0. | returns `0` |\n| E5 | `match` | `bins == 0`. VLAs are zero-length; `total` loops 0×, so gate is `0.0 < threshold*0.0`; `memcpy(v,src,0)` is a no-op; `smoothen` loops 0×; **`differentiate` stores `v[-1] = 0` out of bounds** (`match.c:25`, unguarded). | no crash (the OOB store lands in `match`'s own zero-sized alloca scratch, below `%rsp`); returns `(0.0 >= threshold)`, i.e. `1` iff `threshold <= 0.0`, `0` if `threshold > 0.0` or NaN |\n| E6 | `spectral_contrast` | `length == 0` | all three loops run 0×; `sqrt(0.0)` never used; returns `+0.0`; both arrays untouched |\n| E7 | `spectral_contrast` | `length < 0` (e.g. `-1`, `-1000`, `INT_MIN`) — no validation; every loop guard `i < length` is false at `i = 0` | returns `+0.0`; both arrays untouched; **no** crash |\n| E8 | `match` | `bins < 0` — no validation. Gate passes (totals are `0.0`), then `preprocess` calls `memcpy(v, source, length * sizeof(*v))` where `length * sizeof` converts a **negative int to `size_t`** ⇒ ~2^64-sized copy. | **segfault** (UB in the C; not a value the C \"returns\"). Documented, not asserted for value equality; see `tests/errors.rs::e8_negative_bins_documented` |\n| E9 | `spectral_contrast` / `normalize` | zero magnitude: `dot_product(v,v,length) == 0` ⇒ `magnitude == 0.0` ⇒ `v[i] /= 0.0` with **no guard** (`spectral_contrast.c:13`). Happens for an all-`+0.0`/`-0.0` array, and *always* inside `match` when `preprocess` output is all zeros (e.g. constant input spectra). | `0.0/0.0` ⇒ indefinite QNaN `0xFFC00000` (f32); `x/0.0` for `x != 0` ⇒ `±inf` (f32). Then `dot_product` of those ⇒ `NaN`. `match` then returns `0` (E4). No crash. |\n| E10 | `spectral_contrast` / `normalize` | negative-`dot_product` self-product is impossible in exact math, but with the f32 reinterpretation `sum` can become `-inf`/NaN ⇒ `sqrt` of NaN/negative | `sqrt(NaN)` ⇒ quieted NaN; `sqrt` never sees a negative finite value because `a[i]*a[i] >= 0`, but it can see `NaN`. Propagates; no crash |\n| E11 | `spectral_contrast` | `a[i]` / `b[i]` bytes decode to an **f32 signalling NaN** (`0x7FBFFFFF` etc.). No check; `mulss`/`cvtss2sd`/`divsd` quiet it. | quieted NaN propagated (payload rules in `src/lib.rs`); result NaN; no trap (SSE exceptions masked) |\n| E12 | `spectral_contrast` | aliased arguments `spectral_contrast(v, v, length)` — permitted by C (no `restrict`), so `normalize` runs **twice** on the same buffer | second `normalize` divides the already-normalized data by ≈1.0; result ≈ `1.0`; buffer mutated twice |\n| E13 | `spectral_contrast` | partially overlapping arguments, e.g. `spectral_contrast(v, v+1, length-1)` | well-defined in C: `normalize(a)` completes before `normalize(b)` starts; must match byte-for-byte |\n| E14 | `match`, `spectral_contrast` | **null pointer** with `length`/`bins` `<= 0`: `match(NULL,NULL,0,t)` and `spectral_contrast(NULL,NULL,0)`. Loops never dereference. (`bins > 0` with NULL is an unavoidable segfault in both and is not a comparable value.) | `spectral_contrast(NULL,NULL,0)` ⇒ `+0.0`; `match(NULL,NULL,0,t)` ⇒ `(0.0 >= threshold)`; no crash |\n| E15 | `match` | out-of-range *\"enum\"* value across the FFI boundary. The API has no `enum` type; the only non-pointer, non-float parameter is `int bins`, whose entire `int` range is accepted without validation. Boundary ints: `INT_MIN`, `-1`, `0`, `1`, `INT_MAX`. For `spectral_contrast` all five are safe (E6/E7). For `match`, `bins >= 1` allocates a `bins`-element VLA, so `INT_MAX` ⇒ stack overflow. | `spectral_contrast`: `INT_MIN`/`-1`/`0` ⇒ `+0.0`. `match`: `0` ⇒ E5; `INT_MIN`/`-1` ⇒ E8 segfault; `INT_MAX` ⇒ stack-overflow segfault. Documented, not value-asserted |\n| E16 | `match` | `bins == 1`: `differentiate` writes `v[0] = 0` (the `for` loop body never runs since `1 - 1 == 0`), so both preprocessed buffers are all-zero ⇒ E9 zero-magnitude path. `spectral_contrast` reads **1 f32** out of the 2 f32 slots of the single `double`. | `match` returns `0` unless the gate already returned `0`; specifically `contrast` is NaN ⇒ `>= threshold` false ⇒ `0` |\n| E17 | `match` | `bins` odd, so `spectral_contrast` reads `bins` f32 elements = `bins/2` doubles + the low half of one more — never past the end of the `bins`-double buffer (`bins <= 2*bins`). Not an error, but it is the boundary the type confusion sits on and it is the one unchecked-length interaction in the library. | in bounds; no crash; value must match |\n| E18 | `smoothen` | window clamped at the array end (`i + j < length`) while the divisor stays `N_SMOOTH` (16), unguarded — the last `min(15, length-1)` outputs are attenuated by `(length-i)/16`. No error is raised. | attenuated tail, bit-exact; applies whenever `length < 16` to *every* element |\n\n## Non-rows (checked and confirmed absent)\n\n`grep` found no: allocation-failure path (no `malloc`), no integer-overflow\ncheck, no length maximum, no alignment check, no `restrict` qualifier, no\n`const` qualifier, no return-code enum, no output parameter, no logging. The\nlibrary validates nothing. Rows E5–E17 are precisely the boundaries a caller\ncan hit *because* nothing is validated.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":35,"oldLines":27,"newStart":35,"newLines":30,"lines":[" "," ## The table"," ","-| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |","-|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|","-| E1 | `match` | `total(test,bins) < threshold * total(reference,bins)` — the energy gate at `match.c:37`, the library's only explicit `return 0`. Reached e.g. with `test` energy strictly below `threshold *` `reference` energy. | returns `0` (int), **before** any preprocessing; `test`/`reference` untouched |","-| E2 | `match` | gate operand is NaN, so the `<` is unordered: `total(test,bins)` is NaN, or `threshold` is NaN, or the product is NaN. `comisd`+`jbe` ⇒ unordered does **not** take the `return 0` branch. | gate does **not** reject; execution falls through to preprocessing |","-| E3 | `match` | `threshold * total(reference,bins)` = `inf * 0` or `0 * inf` (invalid op) ⇒ product is the x86 indefinite QNaN `0xFFF8000000000000` | gate unordered ⇒ falls through (same as E2) |","-| E4 | `match` | final `spectral_contrast(t,r,bins) >= threshold` is false or unordered (contrast NaN, or `threshold` NaN, or `threshold` = `+inf`). `comisd`+`setae`: unordered ⇒ CF=1 ⇒ 0. | returns `0` |","-| E5 | `match` | `bins == 0`. VLAs are zero-length; `total` loops 0×, so gate is `0.0 < threshold*0.0`; `memcpy(v,src,0)` is a no-op; `smoothen` loops 0×; **`differentiate` stores `v[-1] = 0` out of bounds** (`match.c:25`, unguarded). | no crash (the OOB store lands in `match`'s own zero-sized alloca scratch, below `%rsp`); returns `(0.0 >= threshold)`, i.e. `1` iff `threshold <= 0.0`,