{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_554voswr75hwhhnornzht2qowk4kegpg3tiawjxkrs6qed3mtovq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **Two real bugs found and fixed in the Rust translation.**\n\n## Bugs fixed\n\n**1. Wrong SSE NaN-payload operand roles (`src/lib.rs`)** — the crate's own comments claimed GCC uses the accumulator as the `addsd` destination. The actual disassembly of the canonical `.so` shows the opposite: the freshly loaded **element** is the destination, and in `dot_product` **`b[i]`** is the `mulss` destination. Since the `float_t` type confusion makes NaN-valued f32 elements common (~1 in 256 random f64 mantissas decode to an f32 NaN), this diverged on the very first NaN input:\n\n```\nspectral_contrast(a=[7fde565b], b=[fff30a1d], 1)\n  C = fffe6143a0000000   Rust = 7ffbcacb60000000   (before)\n```\n\nFixed in `total`, `smoothen` and `dot_product`.\n\n**2. `match(_, _, 0, _)` documented as harmless — it is fatal.** The comment claimed `differentiate`'s unguarded `v[-1] = 0` \"lands in unused scratch space.\" Measured: with `bins == 0` both zero-length VLAs sit at `%rsp`, so `v[-1]` is `%rsp - 8` — **`preprocess`'s return address**. C exits 139 (SIGSEGV) for every `threshold`. Reclassified from the configuration surface (`CONFIGS.md` C15) to the error surface (`ERRORS.md` E5), with a child-process test that asserts the crash.\n\nAlso fixed: `Cargo.toml` did not parse (`[lib] name` contained hyphens); `i + j` / `length - 1` now use wrapping arithmetic to match `add %edx,%eax` / `sub $0x1,%eax` and avoid debug-build panics on `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`.\n\n## Artifacts (`translation/`)\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` diff — **0 missing**, 0 unresolved non-runtime symbols |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 18 rows, all `[x]` — including the reclassified crash rows |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 32 rows, all `[x]` + row→test map |\n| `tests/` | 49 differential tests, both `.so`s via `libloading` only |\n| `run_all.sh` | full mechanical sweep → **ALL CHECKS PASSED** |\n\n## Gate\n\n- Symbol diff empty; both feature combinations (`<default>`, `--no-default-features` — no `[features]` table, no `cfg(feature)`, no `#ifdef`).\n- All 32 `CONFIGS.md` + 18 `ERRORS.md` rows pass; **2,000,000-case** fixed-seed soak byte-identical.\n- No binary target exists in `CMakeLists.txt` (library only), so the stdout item is vacuous.\n\n**One irreducible limit, inherent to the C:** the NaN *payload* `spectral_contrast` returns isn't determined by the source. `-O0` and `-O1+` disagree, so no translation can match both. The prescribed build (`cmake ..` with no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`) is `-O0`, and that's what this matches exactly. Everything the C actually specifies matches at `-O0/-O1/-O2/-O3/-Os`: every `match` row and every error row, verified across all five."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":198245,"cache_read_input_tokens":3501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":198245,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ce1be1d-a5a4-493e-9931-fa82fd487ae7","uuid":"ef62d6ba-0d01-413b-ae9f-abe1a7d50b74","timestamp":"2026-09-05T13:01:07.491Z"}
